From b6f362adad19544ca4525978a842ac2e6f04f5b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homar <homar@local>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:05:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] homar app icons: icons and widget previews for the desktop
 editor

The desktop's home-screen editor shows the phone's real icons. Two new
commands in app/lawnchair/omalawn/AppIcons.kt:

- launcher.app_icons {components?, size?, keys_only?}: for each launcher
  activity (all when components is empty) its label, a key and a PNG
  (base64) drawn like a workspace icon: the bitmap from Lawnchair's icon
  cache (icon pack, shape, adaptive wrapping), read on the model thread,
  drawn through newIcon(context, true) as BubbleTextView does, so themed
  icons show when they are on.
- launcher.widget_previews {providers?, size?, keys_only?}: each widget
  provider's preview image, or its icon when it has none, fitted into
  size x size.

The key changes when the picture would: the app's version and update
time, Lawnchair's version and icon settings (shared prefs with "icon" or
"adaptive" in the name, the icon_shape keys), the night mode (themed
icons follow it) and the size. keys_only answers without drawing, so the
desktop asks for pictures only for what it has not cached. An answer
stays under the link's 1 MiB line: past 700k characters of base64 the
rest come back with deferred: true and no picture.

Hooks: one line each in OmalawnCommands and in the link's method table.
